.TH HCC2D_STREAMER 1 "August 2026" "HCC2D CLI C Streamer 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hcc2d_streamer \- transfer files through streams of QR or HCC2D symbols
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hcc2d_streamer
[\fIoptions\fR]
\fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBhcc2d_streamer\fR reads a file, optionally compresses it, splits it into
dynamic Reed-Solomon erasure groups, and displays the resulting shards as a
repeating sequence of QR, HCC2D4, or HCC2D8 symbols in an SDL2 window.
The HCC2D Decoder companion app captures the sequence and reconstructs the
original file.
.PP
HCC2DST v2 streams require HCC2D Decoder version 1.2.4 or later.
.PP
The maximum input-file size is 2 MiB (2,097,152 bytes), matching the current
HCC2D Decoder limit.
.PP
Symbols are generated in memory and are not written to temporary image files.
.PP
This public CLI supports only QR, HCC2D4, and HCC2D8 with symbol versions 1 to
40. Experimental HCC2D16 and experimental version 45 are not included.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fBqr\fR|\fBhcc2d4\fR|\fBhcc2d8\fR
Select the symbol family. The default is \fBhcc2d8\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-ec-level\fR \fBL\fR|\fBM\fR|\fBQ\fR|\fBH\fR
Set the error-correction level inside each symbol. The default is \fBM\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fIN\fR
Set the fixed symbol version from 1 to 40. The default is 33.
.TP
\fB\-\-fps\fR \fIN\fR
Set the display rate to 10, 12, 15, or 20 symbols per second. The default is
12. On a 60 Hz display, these rates show each symbol for exactly 6, 5, 4, or
3 refresh cycles, respectively.
.TP
\fB\-\-display\fR \fIN\fR
Select the SDL display index used for window placement and size calculation.
The index must be non-negative; the default is 0. The program reports the
number of available displays if the selected index does not exist.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet-zone\fR \fIN\fR
Set the quiet zone from 0 to 16 modules. The default is 4.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-titlebar\fR
Hide window decorations so that more display height is available to the
symbol.
.TP
\fB\-\-palette-rgb\fR \fILIST\fR
Set a complete custom HCC2D4 or HCC2D8 palette as a quoted list of
semicolon-separated \fIR,G,B\fR triplets. Index 0 must be black and the last
index white.
This option is not valid with QR mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-max-data-shards\fR \fIN\fR
Set the maximum number of data shards in one erasure group, from 1 to 255.
The default is 150.
.TP
\fB\-\-parity-ratio\fR \fIR\fR
Set the ratio of parity shards to data shards, from 0 to 1. The default is
0.70, and up to six decimal places are accepted. For example, 0.70 adds
approximately 70 parity shards per 100 data shards.
If the requested maximum data-shard count would make a group exceed 255 total
shards, the program automatically lowers the effective data-shard limit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show the built-in help text and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Stream a file with the default HCC2D8 profile:
.B hcc2d_streamer document.pdf
.br
Theoretical symbol-layer rate: approximately 0.47 Mbps.
.TP
Stream HCC2D8 version 40 at 15 symbols per second:
.B hcc2d_streamer \-\-mode hcc2d8 \-\-ec-level L \-\-version 40 \-\-fps 15 document.pdf
.br
Theoretical symbol-layer rate: approximately 1.06 Mbps.
.TP
Stream HCC2D4:
.B hcc2d_streamer \-\-mode hcc2d4 \-\-ec-level M \-\-version 30 document.pdf
.br
Theoretical symbol-layer rate: approximately 0.26 Mbps.
.TP
Stream standard QR Codes:
.B hcc2d_streamer \-\-mode qr \-\-ec-level L \-\-version 20 document.pdf
.br
Theoretical symbol-layer rate: approximately 0.08 Mbps.
.PP
These are theoretical symbol-layer rates: the data-codeword capacity after
accounting for the internal QR/HCC2D Reed-Solomon overhead, multiplied by the
selected display rate. They do not subtract application framing or apply the
external erasure-code parity ratio, and therefore are not estimates of useful
file-transfer throughput.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hcc2d_streamer
returns 0 after the window is closed normally and a non-zero status on errors.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hcc2d_streamer
Installed command-line Streamer.
.SH SECURITY
The Streamer performs a local optical transfer and does not upload the input
file. Anyone able to observe and decode enough displayed symbols may recover
the file.
